{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And when his power comes to an end he shall be broken</b> — For it is known that Antiochus fell from the roof and was broken and died. The Gaon [Saadia] said: that two thousand and three hundred are years, and their beginning is from the exile of Egypt. And what reason is there to begin from there, and further, how is it \"evening and morning\"? According to his view this appointed time has already passed many years ago. And what is correct in my eyes: that six years and months Israel stood in the days of Antiochus in great trouble, and so it is written in the book of Yon, and behold this number is days." "And the reason of \"two thousand and three hundred evenings\" — and they are six years of solar years and three months and days of them from lunar years, close to six and a half years; therefore the angel said: \"and the vision of the evening and the morning is true.\" And the meaning is that it is as its literal sense, evening and morning. And were it not that we found this number written and already passed, no person could understand this number; therefore Daniel said: \"and I was astonished at the vision, and there is none who understands.\" And indeed the words of the end of redemption are sealed and closed; even Daniel did not know the end, for thus he said: \"and I heard but did not understand.\" And so he said at the end: \"and seal the book until the time of the end,\" and the discerning will understand upon the arrival of the end from the words of the angel."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:34.180678802Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}